# The lower bound of a ball with a one-limb center, as a number of T (milestone2.md, "One
# enclosure interface", the row of lower_as and upper_as, and "The empty set and the whole line"):
# for a finite ball RD(c - r), the largest number of T not above every member, in the
# format with overflow; the whole line gives -inf (0 - inf rounded down), and the empty ball
# +inf, by the select on the radius, which is a NaN exactly for the empty ball.
kernel:        ball_lower_as_1
input:         stored c
input:         stored r
output:        l
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       set_bound l below x x=c,r tight=rounded
min_precision: 2
source:        the center minus the radius, rounded down (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   l is selected after the test of the radius that tells the empty ball; set_bound states what comes out for each state of the ball

t  = sub_down_1(c, r)
ne = eq(r, r)
l  = select(ne, t, const inf)
